{"statement_verdicts":[],"assumption_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"ass:state-incidence","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"StateIncidence r := ∀ t : blackNonOuter (A), (r t).val ∈ T.faceVertices t. Assignment has type A → X (nonRoot), and faceVertices of a triangle face is the set of vertices of that triangle. The extra clause for isolated vertices adds nothing for a triangle. So this is exactly r(t) ∈ V(t) for every t ∈ A, and it matches def:state."},{"obj_id":"ass:pair-distinct","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"PairDistinct r s := ∀ t : A, r.val t ≠ s.val t. Inequality of elements of the subtype X is the same as inequality of the underlying vertices, so this is exactly r(t) ≠ s(t) for every t ∈ A (def:pair)."},{"obj_id":"ass:pair-existence","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"PairExists := ∃ r s : State, IsPair r s. IsPair's only field is PairDistinct, which is exactly def:pair: an ordered pair of states with r(t) ≠ s(t) on A. So this is 'at least one pair exists' with no extra content."},{"obj_id":"ass:cancel-cyclic","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"QsCyclic s := ¬(Qs s).IsAcyclic. In Mathlib, IsAcyclic means no cycle exists, so its negation says some cycle exists, i.e. Q_s contains a simple undirected cycle, as the pinned reading ass:pin-1 requires. Qs is the spanning simple graph on all of T's vertices whose edges are the edges opposite s(t) for t ∈ A. A simple graph cannot hold a 2-cycle, but black triangles of a partition coloring share no edge, so no parallel edges arise."},{"obj_id":"ass:root-forest","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"QsForest s := (Qs s).IsAcyclic. A forest is an acyclic graph, so this is exactly 'Q_s is a forest' for the spanning subgraph of opposite edges."}],"substrate_gates":[],"escalate":null}

